  <prompt>
    Make the customerId standard (`^[a-z][a-z0-9]{2,7}$`, docs/architecture/AZURE-RESOURCE-NAMING-CONVENTION.md
    § "The customerId standard") the rule everywhere a provisioning customerId is ASSIGNED: the L2 API, the intake
    schema, the /provision-environment skill, the operator scripts and the registry column. Record the customer's
    full name once on the registry row so an abbreviated id (northwind → nwind) is never re-derived. Bring every test
    fixture and doc that encodes the old kebab-case shape into line.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer on the L2 provisioning control plane. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in ASP.NET Core
    Minimal APIs, Dataverse metadata (Web API EntityDefinitions/Attributes), PowerShell, JSON Schema.
  </role>

  <goal>
    After this task: (1) `POST /api/runs` returns 400 for any customerId that does not match the standard, before any
    registry lookup, Cosmos write or enqueue; (2) `intake.schema.json`, the skill's interactive and batch intake, and
    every operator script `-CustomerId` parameter enforce the same pattern; (3) `sprk_dataverseenvironment.sprk_customerid`
    has MaxLength 8 in the live admin environment and in `scripts/Add-CustomerIdColumn.ps1`; (4) intake captures the
    customer's display name and the placeholder row stores it in `sprk_name` next to the id, so the id↔name decision is
    recorded once; (5) no test fixture, example or template carries a non-compliant customerId except deliberate
    negative cases.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Owner D10 (2026-09-30) adopted unified-access-control-r2's D-14 standard. `customer.bicep` composes
      `take(format('sprk-{0}-{1}-kv', customerId, environmentName), 24)`; a 10-char id with env `staging` yields a name
      ending in a hyphen, which Azure rejects. The storage name strips hyphens, so `acme-x` and `acmex` collide silently.
      ARM cannot enforce the character rule (no @pattern), and a Dataverse text column cannot either — intake code is the
      only enforcement point (INCOMING §2a). Today the L2 API only checks non-blank (`RunsEndpoints.cs:382-385`); the
      schema and skill still say kebab-case 3–32 (`intake.schema.json:12-13`, SKILL.md Step 1a ~line 677); the column is
      MaxLength 64 (`scripts/Add-CustomerIdColumn.ps1:99-105`, live spaarkedev1 = NVARCHAR(64)). Live registry check
      2026-09-30 (spaarkedev1): NO row has a sprk_customerid value; one stale placeholder row named `trial-2026-08-18`
      (created 2026-08-18, no URL/type/customerId). The BFF already enforces the pattern at runtime
      (`src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Configuration/CustomerIdResolver.cs:86`, `CustomerIdPattern`), but the control plane
      does not reference the BFF and must not.
      Adjacent drift found while scoping (plan G22): T224 renamed the `sprk_tenancymodel` option labels to Model1/Model2
      in `scripts/Extend-DataverseEnvironmentSchema-v3.3.ps1` but never applied them — live spaarkedev1 still shows
      Model1Shared/Model2Dedicated. Same table, same operator session, so it is folded into this task's live step.
    </background>
