  <constraints>
    <constraint source="INCOMING-CUSTOMERID-STANDARD §2a + naming doc (BINDING)">
      Every validation point added or changed in this task uses exactly `^[a-z][a-z0-9]{2,7}$` — no trimming, no
      lower-casing, no auto-abbreviation of the submitted value (reject, never repair). Cite the naming doc rather than
      restating the derivation. Min-3 stays (it is in the pattern) but no new code treats it as more than the pattern.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-001 / ADR-008 / .claude/constraints/api.md">
      The CreateRun rejection uses the endpoint's existing `BadRequest(httpContext, ...)` ProblemDetails helper (400,
      correlationId extension) and runs before the registry lookup (REG-07), the CustomerRunGuard, any Cosmos write and
      any enqueue. No new middleware or filter.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10 + plan boundary">
      The control plane MUST NOT reference `Sprk.Bff.Api`. The only BFF change allowed is the doc comment at
      `DataverseEnvironmentRecord.cs:70` (comment-only; publish size N/A) and BFF test fixtures listed in the inventory.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038 §7 + tests/CLAUDE.md">
      Fixture edits preserve each test's intent: a deliberate mismatch test keeps a DIFFERENT compliant id; deliberate
      blank / malformed inputs stay malformed. No test is deleted, skipped or narrowed.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-11 + owner directive (live envs)">
      Live Dataverse changes use the operator's OWN identity, only against spaarkedev1 (the registry/admin environment),
      and only the three changes named in step 6. Never delete a registry row; deactivate. Never drop or recreate the
      `sprk_customerid_key` alternate key or the column.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="manifest/prereqs CI">
      `scripts/provisioning-prereqs/validate.ps1` and `npx ajv-cli@5 compile --spec=draft2020 -s scripts/provisioning-prereqs/intake.schema.json` pass.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

