  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Add `CustomerIdStandard` (static, Core/Models): `public const string Pattern = "^[a-z][a-z0-9]{2,7}$";`, a `[GeneratedRegex]`, and `IsValid(string? value)`; XML doc cites the naming doc and `CustomerIdResolver.CustomerIdPattern`. Unit-test it with the case list in acceptance criterion 2.</step>
    <step order="2">CreateRun: after the existing blank check, reject a non-matching customerId with 400 — message: "customerId '{value}' does not match the customerId standard ^[a-z][a-z0-9]{2,7}$ (3-8 lowercase letters/digits, starting with a letter; see AZURE-RESOURCE-NAMING-CONVENTION.md). Abbreviate longer names at intake (northwind → nwind)." Add RunsEndpointsTests cases.</step>
    <step order="3">Schema + defaults: `intake.schema.json` customerId pattern/description/examples; add optional `displayName` (string, 1-200 chars; the customer's full name; defaults to customerId); `context-defaults.dev.json` / `.prod.json` shape text.</step>
    <step order="4">Skill (main session): Step 1a states the rule + abbreviation guidance and validates the entered value with the regex (re-prompt on failure); Step 1 captures `displayName`; the placeholder create writes `sprk_name = displayName` (default customerId) and `sprk_customerid = customerId`; fix the stale examples (`trial-acme-2026-08-18`, "kebab-case" text near the batch-mode and Step 4.0 sections). Leave the `__role-probe__` query value (it is not an intake value).</step>
    <step order="5">Scripts: `[ValidatePattern('^[a-z][a-z0-9]{2,7}$')]` on `-CustomerId` in Provision-Customer.ps1, Decommission-Customer.ps1 (and its `rg-spaarke-[a-z0-9]{3,10}-…` match), Deploy-Release.ps1, Initialize-ReportingCustomer.ps1 (examples → compliant), tests/bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1. `Add-CustomerIdColumn.ps1`: MaxLength 8 + description citing the standard. Leave `stacks/model1-*.bicep` (retired by T225a).</step>
    <step order="6">LIVE spaarkedev1 (prescriptive order; operator identity; read back after each): (a) re-confirm no row has a non-empty sprk_customerid (if one does → escalation trigger 2); (b) set `sprk_customerid` MaxLength 64 → 8; (c) deactivate (statecode=1, statuscode=2) the stale `trial-2026-08-18` placeholder row — do not delete; (d) G22: set `sprk_tenancymodel` option labels 0 → "Model1", 1 → "Model2" with the descriptions already in `Extend-DataverseEnvironmentSchema-v3.3.ps1` (labels only; values unchanged). Record before/after in notes.</step>
    <step order="7">Fixture sweep per the inventory in notes; update docs: `provisioning-runs/_templates/intake.md` (rule + pointer + displayName meaning), DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE line ~147 ("3-10 alphanumeric" → the standard), `DataverseEnvironmentRecord.cs:70` comment.</step>
    <step order="8">Verify: builds 0/0 (ControlPlane Api/Worker/Tests, Sprk.Bff.Api, BFF unit tests project); ControlPlane.Tests only the 6 CustomerRunGuard baseline failures; BFF tests for touched files pass; ArchTests 337/337; validate.ps1 + ajv compile OK; grep shows no non-compliant customerId literal outside the deliberate-negative list.</step>
    <step order="9">Step 9.5 gates; POML completed + notes; TASK-INDEX `✅ [done]`; plan §3 (INCOMING-CUSTOMERID-STANDARD row) + §4 G22 + §7 T237; current-task.md; one commit; push.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Dataverse refuses the MaxLength decrease on `sprk_customerid` (e.g. because the column backs the `sprk_customerid_key` alternate key) — STOP and report the exact error; do not drop/recreate the key or column, do not widen the code rule.</trigger>
    <trigger>Any live registry row has a non-empty `sprk_customerid` (none did on 2026-09-30) — STOP: re-issuing a real id touches the alternate key and possibly Azure resource names; owner decides.</trigger>
    <trigger>Any code reads the `sprk_tenancymodel` formatted LABEL text (rather than the 0/1 value) and expects the old names — STOP before relabelling and report the consumer.</trigger>
    <trigger>A script's `-CustomerId` turns out to be a different identifier than the Spaarke customerId (e.g. a reporting-only name) — leave it, note why, continue.</trigger>
    <trigger>Changing a fixture value would change what the test proves (e.g. a length- or hyphen-dependent assertion) — keep it, list it in notes as a deliberate case.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>`src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Configuration/CustomerIdResolver.cs:86` (`CustomerIdPattern`) — the only regex for the standard; it lives in the BFF. `grep -rn "a-z0-9" src/server/services` finds no control-plane equivalent.</existing>
    <extension>No — the control plane does not and must not reference `Sprk.Bff.Api` (BFF/provisioning boundary, CLAUDE.md §10), so the BFF type cannot be reused; a small Core type is the one shared point for the API and any later handler check.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>`POST /api/runs` accepts `acme-x` (silent storage-account collision with `acmex`) and 9-10-char ids (`customer.bicep` Key Vault name truncated or ending in a hyphen → H2a deployment fails late with an opaque Azure error).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

