  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">1. `POST /api/runs` with a customerId that fails the pattern returns 400 ProblemDetails whose detail names the value and the standard, and creates no Cosmos run, registry call or Service Bus message; a compliant id proceeds exactly as before. Tests cover: accepted `abc` (3) and `abcdefgh` (8); rejected `ab` (2), `abcdefghi` (9), `Acme` (uppercase), `acme-x` (hyphen), `1acme` (leading digit), `acme_x` (underscore), ` acme` (leading space — not trimmed). The existing blank → 400 test still passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">2. `CustomerIdStandard.IsValid` returns true for `abc`, `acme`, `nwind`, `abcdefgh`, `a1b2c3` and false for null, empty, `ab`, `abcdefghi`, `Acme`, `acme-x`, `1acme`, `acme_x`, ` acme`, `acme `. `CustomerIdStandard.Pattern` equals the BFF's `CustomerIdResolver.CustomerIdPattern` string (checked by reading both into the task notes; the case list matches the BFF resolver's negative cases).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">3. `intake.schema.json`: customerId `pattern` = `^[a-z][a-z0-9]{2,7}$`, description cites the naming doc, every example body uses a compliant id; optional `displayName` (string, 1-200) documented as the customer's full name recorded on the registry row. `npx ajv-cli@5 compile --spec=draft2020` succeeds; `validate.ps1` passes; `IntakeSchemaProfileParityTests` pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">4. SKILL.md: Step 1a validates the entered id against the regex and re-prompts with abbreviation guidance; batch mode relies on the updated schema; Step 1 collects `displayName`; the placeholder create writes `sprk_name = displayName` (default customerId) and `sprk_customerid = customerId`; no example or prose in the skill describes customerId as kebab-case or 3-32 chars. `.claude/CHANGELOG.md` has an entry.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">5. Each script listed in step 5 rejects a non-compliant `-CustomerId` at parameter binding (or the escalation-trigger-4 note explains why one was left); `Add-CustomerIdColumn.ps1` creates MaxLength 8.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">6. Live spaarkedev1, read back after the change: `sprk_customerid` MaxLength = 8; the `trial-2026-08-18` row is Inactive (still present); `sprk_tenancymodel` labels are Model1 (0) / Model2 (1). Before/after recorded in notes. (If an escalation trigger fires, the criterion is met by the recorded escalation instead.)</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">7. No customerId literal in the inventoried test files, script examples, schema examples, the skill or `intake.md` violates the pattern, except the deliberate negative inputs listed in notes; tests that compared two different customers still compare two different compliant ids; generated smoke/seam ids are compliant (e.g. a letter prefix + 7 lowercase hex chars).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">8. Builds 0 warnings / 0 errors (ControlPlane Api, Worker, Tests; Sprk.Bff.Api; BFF unit test project); ControlPlane.Tests failures = exactly the 6 `CustomerRunGuardModulePostConfigureTests`; touched BFF tests pass; ArchTests 337/337.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">9. Test scope: cover the stated contract (criteria 1-2) plus the edge cases named there. Fixture edits are value replacements, not new tests. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">10. Step 9.5 code-review + adr-check run; findings dispositioned in completion notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

